(p/'finance/MODEL.md').write_text('''# Editable financing assumptions
Planning date 2026-11-09. No agreed terms, valuation validation or financial forecast. Edit assumptions.json, then rerun scripts/appendix.py to update machine-readable assets and scenarios.csv, or use the browser calculator and export JSON for review. Canonical model is finance/assumptions.json; browser exports are separate what-if files. Narrative budget text describes the original $6M case and must be reconciled after editing.

$6M allocation: $3.30M engineering (55%), $0.60M infrastructure (10%), $0.60M distribution (10%), $0.60M operations (10%), $0.90M reserve (15%). Operating spend $5.10M / 24 = $212,500/month average. Gross capital / 24 = $250,000 including reserve. Founder base $300K for 24 months, plus illustrative 25% payroll burden = $375K, included in engineering, not added twice. Remaining engineering $2.925M supports, for example, 12.19 engineer-years at $240K fully loaded. That is an average of 6.09 engineers over two years; hiring ramps and cash timing must be modeled before commitments.

Illustrative quarterly non-reserve spend: Q1 $350K, Q2 $450K, Q3 $550K, Q4 $650K, Q5 $700K, Q6 $750K, Q7 $800K, Q8 $850K = $5.10M. Reserve $900K remains. No revenue offsets assumed. Costs vary with location, payroll burdens and compute demand. $3M scope reduces hiring and commercial concurrency; $8M/$10M expand execution capacity, not merely runway promises. Founder compensation held constant across scenarios, not a fixed percentage.

At fixed illustrative $30M post-money, ownership for $3M/$6M/$8M/$10M is 10%/20%/26.67%/33.33%. Actual SAFE conversion, option pools, other convertibles and later dilution can differ. Subsequent 20% dilution changes a 20% holding to 16%. Neither cap nor valuation is negotiated.

Pricing hypotheses: individual open tooling; team $24K/year; enterprise $60K/year, excluding execution pass-through charges. No validated willingness to pay. Target count 2,000 × $24K = $48M annual serviceable scenario; 100 × $24K = $2.4M attainable milestone scenario; 10,000 × $60K = $600M longer-term expansion scenario, not additive to the initial pool. Counts are unsourced planning assumptions, not externally measured market size.
''')
caps=json.loads((p/'research/capabilities.json').read_text())
sections=[]
def sec(id,title,body):sections.append(f'<section id="{id}"><span class="eyebrow">DILIGENCE / {len(sections)+1:02}</span><h2>{title}</h2>{body}</section>')
sec('architecture','One ecosystem. Separate responsibilities.','''<p>The architecture below is a composition map. Solid associations describe documented responsibilities; the hosted operating layer is proposed. No automatic universal integration or policy enforcement is claimed.</p><div class="architecture"><details open><summary>Clarity: intent and outcome</summary><p>Kujo compiler/runtime runs programs. Spec defines task contracts. Eval executes configured checks. Language capability policies do not replace container or operating-system boundaries.</p></details><details><summary>Context: inputs and records</summary><p>MCP exposes configured tools/resources. CaseFile captures commands and logs. RunLedger stores supplied results and Git context. Watchdog records supported telemetry and estimated costs.</p></details><details><summary>Control: state and execution</summary><p>Dispatch persists workflow state and approvals. Workcell applies supported host/container limits. ShipCheck checks release-readiness signals. Human reviewers retain authority.</p></details><details><summary>Proposed commercial layer</summary><p>Hosted execution, evidence retention, team review and organization governance. Product integration, multi-tenant isolation, service operations and commercial validation remain work to fund.</p></details></div>''')
sec('maturity','Capability and maturity matrix','<div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Component</th><th>Capability / maturity</th><th>Boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join(f'<tr><th><a href="{c["source"]}">{h(c["project"])}</a><br><small>{c["id"]}</small></th><td>{h(c["capability"])}<br><small>{h(c["status"])}</small></td><td>{h(c["limitations"])}</td></tr>' for c in caps)+'</tbody></table></div>')
files=sorted((p/'assets/evidence').rglob('*')); before=next((x for x in files if x.name=='case.json' and 'before' in str(x)),None);after=next((x for x in files if x.name=='case.json' and 'after' in str(x)),None)
links=''.join(f'<a href="{h(str(x.relative_to(p/"assets")))}">{h(str(x.relative_to(p/"assets/evidence")))}</a>' for x in files if x.is_file())
sec('evidence','Inspect the recorded run','''<p><strong>Authentic local execution; deliberately seeded fixture.</strong> The assistant authored a small coding task, recorded its failure, corrected the formula and ran the checks. This is not a customer incident, live production agent run or independent attestation.</p><div class="evidence-nav"><button data-evidence="request">Request</button><button data-evidence="diff">Code change</button><button data-evidence="before">Failed command</button><button data-evidence="after">Passed command</button><button data-evidence="eval">Evaluation</button><button data-evidence="decision">Decision</button></div><pre id="evidence-output" tabindex="0" aria-label="Selected execution artifact">Select an artifact to inspect it.</pre><p>CaseFile captures command exit status and bounded output. Eval checks the explicit conditions. Files are trusted-local artifacts; SHA-256 detects changes relative to this manifest, not host compromise.</p><details><summary>All original artifacts and reproduction files</summary><div class="file-list">'''+links+'''</div></details>''')
sec('benchmarks','A correctness fixture, not a performance claim','''<p>Method: Node assertions check 6/30 = 20% and 3/30 = 10%; the initial denominator intentionally adds the raise and fails. CaseFile captures both executions. Eval runs the assertion command and checks the corrected source expression. Observed result: two configured Eval checks passed, with the earlier assertion failure retained.</p><p>Reproduce with <code>python3 scripts/record-demo.py</code> from the source deck, using the sibling CaseFile, Eval and Kujo 1.9.0 checkout. This overwrites the recorded fixture artifacts; retain the original before comparing runs. Timings are recorded but not a statistically meaningful benchmark. No competitor benchmark, latency advantage, comprehensive correctness or security certification is claimed.</p><p>Future benchmark plan: publish fixed repositories, pinned environments, task corpus, failure taxonomy, complete attempts, repeated seeds and independent reproduction. Measure reviewer time, evidence completeness and failure recovery alongside task success.</p>''')
comp=[('Execution boundaries','Existing agent environment controls; inspect configuration','Application/host responsibility','Workcell documented OCI bounds'),('Evidence provenance','Repository/session history','Checkpointed state and traces','CaseFile command bundles; RunLedger supplied receipts'),('Reproducibility','Depends on task, dependencies and environment','Requires deterministic/idempotent design','Pinned fixtures and exported artifacts; host trust remains'),('Recovery','Product/workflow specific','Checkpoint recovery documented','Dispatch persisted state; Workcell scoped recovery'),('Policy enforcement','Organization and agent settings','Application-defined controls','Specific tool contracts, not universal language enforcement'),('Release verification','Git review and CI ecosystem','Application-defined','Eval + ShipCheck checks; human decision'),('Integration depth','Strong existing developer distribution','Broad agent application ecosystem','Native language/tooling cohesion; hosted layer proposed'),('Language support','Existing repositories','Python/JS ecosystems','Kujo tooling can inspect non-Kujo application code')]
sec('competition','Strong alternatives define the bar','<p>Representative comparison, source/documentation review dated 2026-11-09, not hands-on parity testing. <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/concepts/copilot-surfaces/copilot-on-github">GitHub Copilot</a> and <a href="https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/langgraph/persistence">LangGraph</a> already offer substantial capability. Observability systems such as <a href="https://opentelemetry.io/docs/">OpenTelemetry</a> standardize telemetry; CI systems such as <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/actions">GitHub Actions</a> execute workflow checks. Kujo should complement or replace specific responsibilities only after evidence.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Coding agents / existing CI</th><th>Orchestration frameworks</th><th>Kujo documented scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join(f'<td>{h(c)}</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in comp)+'</tbody></table></div><p>Potential defensibility: stable evidence contracts, integration quality, reproducible operations and retained developer use. These are future advantages to earn. Open interfaces reduce lock-in and ease adoption; no exclusive technology moat is asserted.</p>')
sec('market','Edit the bottom-up assumptions','''<p>All counts and contract values are unvalidated planning assumptions. The model estimates a narrow organization-level service opportunity, not the entire AI industry.</p><div class="inputs"><label>Initial organizations<input id="organizations" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="2000"></label><label>Annual contract, USD<input id="acv" type="number" min="0" max="10000000" value="24000"></label><label>Attainable customers<input id="customers" type="number" min="0" max="1000000" value="100"></label></div><output id="market-output" aria-live="polite"></output><p>Expansion scenario: 10,000 organizations × $60K = $600M annual pool. This is a separate, longer-term hypothesis, not additive TAM. Validate organization counts, budget ownership, competition, retention and willingness to pay.</p>''')
sec('commercial','Proposed pricing needs customer evidence','''<div class="columns"><div><h3>Developer</h3><p>Open local tooling. Adoption measured by successful and repeated evidence runs.</p></div><div><h3>Team: $24K / year</h3><p>Hypothesis for hosted retention, shared review and team controls. Execution usage may be separate.</p></div><div><h3>Enterprise: $60K / year</h3><p>Hypothesis for governance, deployment support and organization controls. No validated pricing or contracts.</p></div></div><p>Commercial validation sequence: instrument active repositories → investigate repeated use → recruit design partners → paid pilots → retention and expansion. Infrastructure cost, support load and gross margin require actual usage data.</p>''')
sec('funding','Funding scenarios and dilution','''<p>Working scenario: $6M at $30M post-money. These are planning inputs, not agreed terms or validated valuation. Simplified ownership = raise ÷ post-money; SAFE mechanics, option pools and other instruments can change outcomes.</p><div class="inputs"><label>Raise<select id="raise"><option value="3000000">$3M</option><option value="6000000" selected>$6M</option><option value="8000000">$8M</option><option value="10000000">$10M</option></select></label><label>Post-money USD<input id="postmoney" type="number" min="1000000" max="1000000000" value="30000000"></label><label>Runway months<input id="months" type="number" min="1" max="120" value="24"></label></div><output id="funding-output" aria-live="polite"></output><div id="budget" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scenario allocation table"></div><button id="export">Export current assumptions JSON</button><p>At fixed $30M post-money: $3M → 10%; $6M → 20%; $8M → 26.67%; $10M → 33.33%. A later round that dilutes all holders by 20% reduces a 20% holding to 16%.</p><p>$3M prioritizes one flagship workflow and a smaller team. $6M supports parallel runtime, execution and developer experience work. $8M/$10M permit more integration and commercial capacity, conditional on evidence of demand.</p>''')
sec('budget','Twenty-four-month operating plan','''<p>$6M case: $3.30M engineering; $600K infrastructure; $600K distribution; $600K operations; $900K reserve. Non-reserve operating average: $212,500/month. Gross capital divided by 24 months: $250,000/month, including reserve.</p><p>Founder base: $150K/year, or $300K over two years. Illustrative 25% payroll burden makes $375K, included in engineering. Remaining engineering: $2.925M; at $240K per engineer-year, approximately 12.19 engineer-years. Location and hiring ramp materially affect this model.</p><div class="table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="group" aria-label="Scrollable data table"><table><thead><tr><th>Quarter</th><th>Operating spend</th><th>Cumulative</th></tr></thead><tbody>'''+''.join(f'<tr><td>Q{i+1}</td><td>${v:,}</td><td>${sum([350000,450000,550000,650000,700000,750000,800000,850000][:i+1]):,}</td></tr>' for i,v in enumerate([350000,450000,550000,650000,700000,750000,800000,850000]))+'''</tbody></table></div><p>Reserve stays $900K. No revenue offset assumed. This simplified allocation is not a monthly cash-flow forecast. Benefits, taxes, legal, security and customer support must be priced before commitments.</p>''')
sec('roadmap','Hire against measurable milestones','''<ol class="roadmap"><li><h3>Months 0–6</h3><p>Hire execution reliability and developer experience engineers; harden one flagship evidence workflow. Publish reproducible benchmark protocol and recruit external reviewers. Proposed target: 10 independently activated teams.</p></li><li><h3>Months 6–12</h3><p>Expand runtime/integration capacity after activation evidence. Proposed targets: 5 design partners, 3 paid pilots and measured four-week retention. Publish all benchmark limitations.</p></li><li><h3>Months 12–24</h3><p>Add customer engineering when support demand is demonstrated. Test repeatable acquisition, renewal and expansion. 100 customers at $24K is a scenario to test, not a committed forecast.</p></li></ol><p>December 2026 campaign is planned. Measure unique activated repositories, successful evidence runs, repeat usage, qualified conversations and paid conversions by cohort. Partnerships are prospective.</p>''')
sec('risks','Technical ambition must survive commercial reality','''<dl><dt>Language adoption</dt><dd>New language adoption may take years. Sell useful workflow infrastructure independently of migration.</dd><dt>Integration complexity</dt><dd>Tools have distinct contracts and runtime pins. Fund one reliable flagship experience before promising seamless coverage.</dd><dt>Trust and security</dt><dd>Editable local evidence is not independent attestation. Hosted custody, tenant isolation and retention need dedicated design and review.</dd><dt>Incumbents</dt><dd>Agents, CI and observability vendors can expand into accountability. Prove lower operational burden and repeat use.</dd><dt>Demand and pricing</dt><dd>No verified customer, retention or revenue data supplied. Validate the beachhead and pricing through actual pilots.</dd><dt>Founder concentration</dt><dd>Broaden maintainership, documentation and release ownership. Confirm contributor attribution and biography before distribution.</dd></dl>''')
sec('sources','Source register and investor follow-up','<p>Research cut: 2026-11-09. Release inventory dated 2026-10-22 is not a blanket current-HEAD guarantee. Full claim register is retained in source at research/CLAIMS.md.</p><ul>'+''.join(f'<li><a href="{c["source"]}">{c["id"]} / {c["project"]} / pinned source</a></li>' for c in caps)+'''<li><a href="https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2026/ai">M03/M04: Stack Overflow 2026 AI survey</a></li><li><a href="https://robertdevore.com/about/">F01: Robert DeVore public biography</a></li><li><a href="https://docs.kujolang.ai/ecosystem/releases/">Release inventory</a></li><li><a href="https://kujolang.ai">Kujo official site</a></li></ul><p>Before investor distribution: supply verified adoption and commercial metrics, confirm founder attribution and contact details, validate pricing/budget assumptions, and obtain financing advice on actual instrument terms. No current customer or investor commitment is represented.</p><a href="https://robertdevore.com/contact/">Investor contact ↗</a>''')
